{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:growth:reconciler","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:85ae566e2ee24ed835809833da9b49d0dffcd3face75bd4d38c58c41f7a4e1f3","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"categorical","probabilities":{"A":0.18,"B":0.48,"C":0.27,"D":0.07}},"questionHash":"sha256:ca2a4311940635fba34c40e7278721deb2f4716732e6011c94e6eb0554263e61","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq6","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"Derived mechanically from MY OWN CQ3 and MY OWN inflation construction under the lexical-priority lock, not assigned freehand, and not averaged. Note first that the three Wave-1 panelists returned B = 49, 50, 50 — a three-point convergence that is the signature of residual-absorption arithmetic applied to three nearly identical CQ3s rather than of three independent views; the Red-Team was right that breaking the CQ3 centre breaks the shape, though his own shape (33/34/28/5) is driven by a China print I reject.\n\nINPUTS. CQ3 = 0.95 / 1.95 / 2.95, implied sigma 0.78. Inflation, from my CQ2 construction mixture (0.68 literal all-38 PPP-GDP, central 2.90%, 5-year-window sigma 0.65; 0.32 advanced-economy construction, central 2.35%, sigma 0.55): P(core >= 2.70% over 2032-36) = 0.68*0.621 + 0.32*0.262 = 0.422 + 0.084 = 0.506 ~ 0.51. P(core < 2.00%) = 0.68*0.083 + 0.32*0.262 = 0.056 + 0.084 = 0.140.\n\nSTEP 1 — A: P(growth >= 2.6%) = 1 - Phi((2.6-1.95)/0.78) = 1 - Phi(0.833) = 0.202. Thinned to 18 for Baumol/Jones upper-tail truncation (clearing 2.6% requires OECD-38 above 2.0%, i.e. ~1.8%/yr per-capita). A = 18. The lock scores A on GROWTH ALONE, so A's \"debt stabilizes via growth\" and \"broad wage gains\" clauses are not priced and A is NOT contaminated by my low CQ1 of 15, which is a claim about the wage DISTRIBUTION, not the growth rate.\n\nSTEP 2 — C: P(growth < 2.0%) = Phi((2.0-1.95)/0.78) = 0.526. Times P(core >= 2.70%) = 0.51 at a dependence factor of 1.00 — justified, not assumed: conditional on low growth, core is HIGHER if the cause is supply walls (grid/care/trades shadow prices) and LOWER if the cause is a demand/capex bust, and under the all-38 construction a global bust also disinflates Turkey and Mexico, so the two dependencies offset. 0.526*0.51 = 0.268 -> C = 27.\n\nSTEP 3 — D: P(growth < 1.7%) = Phi((1.7-1.95)/0.78) = 0.374. Times P(core < 2.00%) = 0.140, times a positive dependence factor of 1.35 (a post-bust demand shortfall produces both coordinates; the BIS Box C labour-income deficit is one mechanism generating both). 0.374*0.140*1.35 = 0.071 -> D = 7. D is crushed not by optimism but by index construction — the literal all-38 GDP-weighted aggregate essentially cannot print core below 2.0% with Turkey and Mexico in it. The Outside-View Scout's 14 and the Inside-View Modeler's 17 are the price of using a Germany-weighted inflation mental model inside an OECD-38 definition; the Red-Team's 5 over-commits to the literal fork. Disjoint from C by construction (core < 2.0 vs >= 2.7), so no lexical double-claiming.\n\nSTEP 4 — B = residual = 100 - 18 - 27 - 7 = 48. Sum = 100 exactly.\n\nCELL-BY-CELL VERIFICATION. P(1.7 <= g < 2.0) = 0.526 - 0.374 = 0.152; its core >= 2.7 slice (0.078) goes to C, the remaining 0.074 stays in B. P(2.0 <= g < 2.6) = 1 - 0.202 - 0.526 = 0.272, ALL to B — the lock routes a stagflationary 2.0-2.6% cell to B because step 2 requires growth < 2.0. P(g < 1.7) = 0.374 splits: 0.191 to C (core >= 2.7), 0.071 to D (core < 2.0 with dependence), 0.112 to B (core between 2.0 and 2.7). C total 0.078 + 0.191 = 0.269 (matches step 2); B total 0.074 + 0.272 + 0.112 = 0.458, plus the 0.02 thinned off A = 0.478 -> 48. The arithmetic closes.\n\nCONSISTENCY CHECK AGAINST MY OWN CQ3: P50 = 1.95% sits inside B's literal 1.7-2.5% band, so B must be modal — it is, at 48, and I have not put most mass on A as the lock warns. A = 18 is within 2 points of the direct normal-tail read off my own CQ3 (20.2%), so no optimism is smuggled in. C + D = 34 against my CQ3's P(growth < 2.0%) = 52.6: the ~19-point gap is precisely the leftover cell (growth < 2.0% with core between 2.0% and 2.7%) that the lock routes to B, which is why B's 48 decomposes as only ~27 from the literal band and ~21 from lock-absorbed cells. A reader scoring this WITHOUT the lock would plausibly report something near A 18 / B 30 / C 32 / D 20; the lock mechanically moves ~18-20 points into B.\n\nCONSISTENCY CHECK AGAINST MY OWN CQ2 (41): CQ2 requires core >= 2.50% over the LONGER 2027-2036 window (my marginal 0.698) AND China < 1.50%. C requires the STRICTER core >= 2.70% over the SHORTER 2032-36 window (my 0.506) and carries no China conjunct, so C is not bounded by 41. Required orderings: 0.506 < 0.698 — satisfied (higher bar, partly offset by greater short-window variance); and C = 27 <= 0.506*0.526 = 26.6 — satisfied, equal by construction. No contradiction. Also note B at 48 sits just above AI-Q6's standalone Jagged Diffusion at 47.2, which is the correct direction of travel: coupling adds the physical/care-scarcity leg to the hyperscaler-rent leg, which is what the barbell describes, so mass should move INTO B, mostly out of A (the growth cap) and partly out of the extreme Hulten tail (the shadow-price surge in bottleneck sectors is itself nominal growth).\n\nEXPLICIT SENSITIVITY: if the resolver adopts an advanced-economy / ex-high-inflation core construction with certainty, C falls to ~0.14 and D rises to ~0.12, with B taking ~0.56. The whole C-vs-D split in my payload rides on the index-construction fork, not on macroeconomics — which is the most uncomfortable fact in this effort, since it means a third of my regime mass turns on a statistical convention rather than on the world.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:55.092Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"The resolving inflation object settles: either the OECD/IMF publishes and analysts adopt an 'OECD advanced' or ex-high-inflation core aggregate as the canonical series, OR Turkey and Mexico core inflation both converge below 4.0%/yr on a 12-month basis — versus the all-38 PPP-GDP-weighted aggregate remaining the only published core object with the high-inflation members carrying full weight.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"This is the single biggest falsifier of MY payload specifically, because 0.68 of my CQ2 conjunct A and essentially the whole C-vs-D split rest on the literal all-38 construction. If an advanced-economy construction becomes canonical (or Turkey/Mexico converge): CQ2 falls from 41 to ~27, CQ6-C falls 27 -> 15, CQ6-D rises 7 -> 13, CQ6-B rises to ~55; gold's regime-C return drops ~3 pp and G7 long nominals' regime-C loss narrows ~2 pp. If the all-38 aggregate remains canonical and prints above 3.0%: CQ2 rises to ~48 and CQ6-C to ~33.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"China official NBS annual real GDP prints below 3.0% for three consecutive calendar years, OR a single print at or below 2.5% — versus the official print holding at or above 3.5% through 2032 with an explicit growth target still in the Five-Year-Plan framing.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My China measured-print centre of 3.20% is the largest single term in CQ3 (0.35 weight) and the number where I split the panel most deliberately. Three sub-3.0% years: CQ3 P50 falls from 1.95 to ~1.72 with the left tail to ~0.8, CQ6-A falls 18 -> 11, CQ6-D rises 7 -> 11, CQ6-B to ~52; China equities and industrial metals drop 2-3 pp in the buildout and ~3 pp in every regime. Holding at or above 3.5%: CQ3 P50 to ~2.10, CQ6-A to ~24, and the Red-Team's thesis is vindicated against mine.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Realized AI capex outcome: either (i) >= 20% of the ~$1.4T commitment stack publicly cancelled, deferred beyond 2032 or written down, or net external AI software/API revenue below 0.5x annualized AI compute D&A for two consecutive reported years — AND, critically, the SIGN of the concurrent measured OECD TFP read in the three years following the impairment.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031 (impairment); Dec 31, 2034 (the TFP read)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"This is the discriminating test between the Wave-1 framing (impairment and weak measured output are the same state) and the Red-Team's capex-supercycle identity (they are complements), and my CQ3 sits deliberately between them. Impairment WITH OECD TFP accelerating above +0.4 pp/yr: CQ3 P50 to ~2.15, CQ6-A to ~26, CQ6-D to ~4, and the AI-complex and private-credit regime-A numbers rise 3-4 pp while power/grid holds. Impairment WITH TFP flat or falling: CQ3 P50 to ~1.75, CQ6-D to ~12, CQ4 P50 down ~25 bp (the investment-demand arrow dies and the demand-shortfall arrow doubles), CQ5 down ~5 (the modal bust is disinflationary and bonds rally).\"} | {\"signpost\":\"US 10y TIPS real yield (FRED DFII10) averages below 1.50% over any rolling 12 months with no active central-bank asset-purchase programme in place, OR the G7 PPP-GDP-weighted 10y real yield averages below 1.20% over any rolling 24 months while US net interest outlays remain at or above 3% of GDP.\",\"by_when\":\"Jun 30, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the monotone debt-supply ratchet plus the window-timed dissaving arrow that are the spine of my CQ4 at 2.30 — it would show the convenience yield intact or a renewed central-bank duration bid. CQ4 moves to roughly 1.25 / 1.65 / 2.60 and the right skew flattens; CQ5 conjunct A falls from 0.46 to ~0.36, taking CQ5 from 32 to ~23 (a basis-point vol index deflates with the yield level); CQ6-D roughly doubles to ~13 at C's expense; G7 long nominals' regime-conditional numbers all shift up ~1.5 pp and gold's regime-C number drops ~2 pp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"The first MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown of >= 20% after Jan 1 2027, and the sign and magnitude of the change in G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal yields between the equity peak and trough dates, paired with the trailing 24-month MOVE average at that point.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Directly tests the +0.50 correlation assumption that is worth 12 of my 32 points on CQ5. Yields rise, or fall by less than 50 bp, through the drawdown: CQ5 rises from 32 to ~48 (the harder conjunct is largely consumed YES and the episode lifts the MOVE average), CQ6-C rises ~5 points, CQ4 P90 rises toward 3.6. A clean flight-to-quality rally of >= 150 bp with trailing MOVE below 90: CQ5 falls to ~18, CQ4 P50 falls ~20 bp and P90 to ~3.0, ~5 points move from CQ6-C into CQ6-D, and the C-versus-D spread on G7 long nominals narrows from 11.5 pp to ~6 pp.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'growth'."}}